WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.620
2018 was a great year for horror movies, but
horror fans have even more to look forward

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.280
to over the next couple of years.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:12.180
Intriguing remakes, sequels to smash hits,
and awesome original projects from beloved

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.540
filmmakers are all making their way to horror
fans in 2019.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:22.020
2017's Happy Death Day was a surprise hit,
a slasher-y take on Groundhog Day that cleverly

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.580
milked its premise for scares and featured
a winning lead performance from Jessica Rothe.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:32.220
The original film's ending saw our heroine's
time loop finally broken, but director Christopher

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.620
Landon has teased that he left some important
details unanswered for the sequel.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.070
Landon will handle scripting duties in addition
to directing this time around, with much of

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.440
the cast set to return.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.780
Rothe has confirmed that the sequel will indeed
pick up right where the first film left off,

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.280
comparing its aesthetic to the Back to the
Future series.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.320
Happy Death Day 2U is expected to hit theaters
on February 14, 2019.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.920
The directing team of Kevin Kolsch and Dennis
Widmyer will helm the upcoming remake of one

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.280
of Stephen King's scariest stories.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.259
Pet Sematary has a killer creative team lined
up, with a script co-written by David Kajganich,

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.160
who wrote this year's Suspiria.

00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:17.100
Jason Clarke will star as beleaguered father
Louis Creed alongside Amy Seimetz as his wife

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.380
Rachel, while John Lithgow will play the Creeds'
neighbor Jud.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.170
The film is set to spook audiences on April
5, which gives you plenty of time to rewatch

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.560
the terrifying 1989 original.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.540
"I finally came back for you Rachel.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:36.760
I'm going to twist your back like mine so
you'll never get out of bed again."

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:42.480
The Curse of La Llorona is an upcoming flick
based on a famous Mexican urban legend surrounding

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.140
the ghost of a mysterious woman.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.400
Director Michael Chaves makes his feature
debut on the film, and early reviews are extremely

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:49.900
positive.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.060
A recent screening at San Diego ComicCon reportedly
brought down the house.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:58.459
The cast is headed up by Linda Cardellini
and Raymond Cruz, a veteran actor who made

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:02.960
an indelible impression as the psychotic Tuco
Salamanca in Breaking Bad.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.440
"Whoooo!

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.480
Damn, man, look at that look!

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:08.820
Hooo!

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.620
Ya s'messed up."

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:17.080
Set in the '70s, the film follows Cardellini
as a widowed social worker who begins to turn

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:22.420
up unsettling similarities between her family's
own tragedy and that of a case she's investigating.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.300
It turns out that both of them may have ties
to the vengeful ghost that the movie is named

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:27.800
after.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.820
The legend of La Llarona is well-known in
Mexican culture, but it's all set to go mainstream

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.840
on April 19, 2019.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:41.780
2004's The Grudge, based on the 2002 Japanese
film Ju-On, didn't exactly wow critics, but

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.100
audiences were scared out of their shorts
by the film's insanely creepy imagery.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:50.800
Next year, audiences will once again have
a chance to get spooked by the vengeful ghosts

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.900
in the upcoming remake.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:57.200
This revival holds significant promise for
one good reason: the involvement of writer-director

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:03.260
Nicolas Pesce, whose 2016 debut feature Eyes
of My Mother was a master class in suspense

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:03.760
and atmosphere.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.700
John Cho and Lin Shaye have joined the cast,
and Sam Raimi, producing the film through

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.580
his Ghost House Pictures imprint, has said
that the new adaptation will draw on the source

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.910
material rather than the 2004 version.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.760
Grudge is scheduled to arrive on June 21.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:22.960
The Conjuring universe just can't seem to
stop expanding outwards.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:28.420
As if the recently released The Nun and the
newly announced The Crooked Man wasn't enough,

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:33.700
a certain supernaturally possessed porcelain
doll will be coming back for Annabelle 3 next

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:34.200
year.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:47.680
Returning screenwriter Gary Dauberman will
be taking over the directing reins as well

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.900
in his debut for the as-yet untitled Annabelle
sequel.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:56.440
The film will see the return of The Conjuring's
psychic investigators Ed and Lorraine Warren,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.840
played by Patrick Wilson and Vera Farmiga.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.540
The Annabelle sequel will reach the big screen
on July 3.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:09.490
From the moment that 2017's It ended, speculation
has been running rampant about a sequel, in

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:13.740
particular, who would fill the roles of the
adult versions of the Losers' Club.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:19.100
Well, wonder no more, since It: Chapter Two
has cast a bevy of excellent actors to play

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.340
the modern-day version of the Losers' Club.

00:04:21.689 --> 00:04:26.920
Jessica Chastain, James McAvoy, and Bill Hader
will all join the cast, while the extremely

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:30.800
talented child actors that anchored the first
It will appear in flashbacks.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:35.820
And of course, Bill Skarsgard will return
as Pennywise, in all of his terrifying glory.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.740
Considering that It shocked everyone by virtue
of being one of the best horror films of the

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:45.379
decade, It: Chapter Two is one of the most
highly anticipated films of the year in any

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.260
genre, but it's got a pretty long wait.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.240
The film is slated to hit theaters on September
6.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:55.060
Escape rooms, in which people pay to figure
out how to liberate themselves from seemingly

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.900
escape-proof places, have become all the rage
in recent years.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:03.260
It's anybody's guess what took Hollywood so
long to come up with a thriller based on the

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:08.409
claustrophobic premise, but finally, here
we are: the aptly titled Escape Room is coming

00:05:08.409 --> 00:05:09.620
our way in 2019.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:14.460
The film brings together six strangers who
receive mysterious invitations to participate

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:19.809
in a hardcore escape room which promises a
$1 million prize to anyone crafty enough to

00:05:19.809 --> 00:05:20.860
complete its challenge.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:25.600
As seen in the harrowing trailer, this is
a room which has ways of making sure nobody

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.420
ever leaves.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.420
Director Adam Robitel, responsible for Insidious:
The Last Key as well as the underrated The

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:37.490
Taking of Deborah Logan, will be at the helm,
with a cast headed up by Deborah Ann Woll,

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:39.300
Taylor Russell, and Logan Miller.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:44.180
Escape Room will make its debut immediately
after the new year, on January 4.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:50.000
2017's Split was a triumphant return to form
for M. Night Shyamalan, following years of

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.300
questionable choices and poor reviews.

00:05:52.629 --> 00:05:57.520
Telling the story of Kevin Wendell Crumb,
a man with 24 distinct personalities, the

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.380
film was a lean, triumphant piece of horror
filmmaking.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:06.800
It also had the old patented Shyamalan twist:
Split revealed itself at the end, via a well-placed

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:11.760
Bruce Willis cameo, as a stealth sequel to
Shyamalan's 2000 hit Unbreakable.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:14.840
"They gave him a funny name, too.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:16.960
What was it?"

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:19.060
"Mr. Glass."

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.440
"Oh yeah."

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.200
Speculation immediately started running rampant
that a third installment was forthcoming,

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:30.520
and it didn't take Shyamalan long to confirm
that Glass, named for Samuel L. Jackson's

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:34.020
villainous Unbreakable character, would reach
theaters in 2019.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:38.900
Jackson himself didn't realize there'd be
a need for him to reprise his role until he

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:44.259
saw Split, but as he told a CinemaCon audience,
he's thrilled about it for a specific reason:

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:48.240
"It's about time I got the title role in my
own motherf—-ing movie."

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:54.419
The trailer features Sarah Paulson as a psychiatrist
specializing in patients who think they're

00:06:54.419 --> 00:06:59.080
superheroes, and considering the superpowered
denizens of the Glass universe, she's probably

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.700
bitten off more than she can chew.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:06.000
It appears Jackson's Mr. Glass will once again
be pulling strings, manipulating Willis' David

00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:11.689
Dunn into a confrontation with the Beast;
McAvoy also returns, as does Split's Anya

00:07:11.689 --> 00:07:12.400
Taylor-Joy.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.600
Glass premieres on January 18.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:22.400
Ever since MGM quietly resurrected the long-defunct
Orion Pictures imprint in 2014, the studio

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.900
has struggled to find an identity.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:28.900
Once responsible for classics such as First
Blood, Bill and Ted's Excellent Adventure,

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.199
and Silence of the Lambs, Orion has spent
the last four years cranking out films which

00:07:33.199 --> 00:07:37.939
have gone largely unnoticed by the general
public, with a couple of exceptions like The

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:43.080
Town that Dreaded Sundown and James Gunn's
2017 thriller The Belko Experiment.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:47.569
These films were fairly well-received and
enjoyed relatively high profiles, and they

00:07:47.569 --> 00:07:51.800
had something else in common, they're among
the studio's only horror pictures making up

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.280
their post-2014 output.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:59.210
Perhaps MGM execs finally noticed the extreme
profitability of the genre in recent years,

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:04.300
because Orion's first effort of 2019, The
Prodigy, looks suitably terrifying.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:08.500
Nicholas McCarthy will direct the film which
looks to bring us a new spin on the Creepy

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:09.620
Child subgenre.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:14.060
Plot details are thin, but the trailer looks
atmospheric as all get-out, and the films

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.460
boasts a pretty stellar cast.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.620
We may have an Omen for a new generation on
our hands.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:23.960
Fox Studios' New Mutants, part of its Marvel/X-Men
universe, has had a troubled history.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:28.980
Originally scheduled for release in April
2018, it was first pushed back ten months

00:08:28.999 --> 00:08:34.539
to February 2019, and then an additional six
months to August, after a series of test screenings

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.000
didn't produce the reaction the studio had
hoped for.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:41.780
Audiences responded well to the film, but
Fox had been shooting for stellar scores,

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:45.520
and decided to take extra time to make New
Mutants as good as it could be.

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:49.900
Since it will be the first true horror film
of the X-Men franchise, this seems like a

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:50.880
reasonable approach.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:55.520
The trailer released ahead of the film's initial
release date promised a claustrophobic, creepy

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.640
good time, but this is a film in which tone
will be everything.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:04.000
The recent deal between Fox and Disney, which
will likely see the X-Men, Fantastic Four,

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:08.030
and Deadpool end up in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe at some point, doesn't seem to have

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.240
affected Fox's plans for New Mutants.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:14.420
The film will appear in theaters too soon
for any cross-pollination to take place, even

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.260
if any was planned.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:20.260
Despite rumors that the long delay and Disney
deal meant the project might be shelved, it's

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.000
been confirmed that New Mutants will arrive
in theaters on August 2.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:29.020
Followed may sound a bit familiar at first,
it's part of the new breed of found footage

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:33.410
flick known as "Screen Life," in which all
of the action takes place within the confines

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:35.240
of computer and smartphone screens.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:39.460
If it seems like a cheap gimmick, consider
that the well-received Unfriended and its

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:44.080
sequel established the viability of the device
as an effective storytelling tool, and the

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:47.240
John Cho-led Searching did even better critically.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:52.960
And despite its similarly tech-y title, Followed
doesn't appear to be simply capitalizing on

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:54.400
this trend, but expanding on it.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:59.790
The film stars Matthew Solomon as a controversial
vlogger who specializes in the "sick and twisted,"

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:05.230
who must up the ante after a benefactor promises
a huge influx of cash if he can pump up his

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.940
subscriber base by Halloween.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:12.460
He plans to get a subscriber bump by livestreaming
his stay in a haunted hotel, which of course

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.840
does not go according to plan.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:19.480
Aside from its Unfriended-meets-1408 premise,
the film innovates by periodically breaking

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:23.920
the immersion to take on the first-person
viewpoint of whoever is watching the video

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:28.140
clips, adding to the growing mystery of just
what exactly is going on here.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:33.180
Followed made its debut in 2018 at the Burbank
International Film Festival, where it took

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:37.520
home the prize for Best Horror Feature, making
it among one of the more intriguing horror

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:40.320
films to watch once an official release date
gets announced.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:46.760
2017's 47 Meters Down was a tense nail-biter
of a deep-sea thriller, featuring Mandy Moore

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:51.310
and Claire Holt as sisters who get way more
than they bargained for on a shark watching

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.500
adventure in Mexico.

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:58.120
The modestly budgeted production turned a
respectable profit, so in 2019 Entertainment

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.440
Studios will bring us 47 Meters Down: The
Next Chapter.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.360
The sequel will feature an all-new group of
characters in a Brazilian locale who run into

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:10.550
some serious shark-based problems while searching
for a lost underground city.

